(7690484, 1260127, 67145, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by streetpigeon:</b></div><hr/><i> This low key image really captures the mental anguish of someone who finds himself in a deep hole.  It must feel that the only way out is to go deeper.  It''s set up and captured beautifully.  The upflung cards, nicely catching the light, are marvelous, putting emotion in motion.  The man''s expression is telling, and driving the entire scene.<br/>Personal second favorite of the challenge. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Rich .. i really liked your comment .. especially the bit where you say "it must feel that the only way out is to go deeper." .. that would apply to many addictions .. :(<br/> <br/>and you know the expression throwing in the towel .. ie. to quit in defeat .. that''s the feeling i get from this pic with the throwing of the cards .. and the man''s expression .. <br/> <br/>many congratulations Girish on fourth and such a wonderful photo with such a powerful message .. :)<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by streetpigeon: This low key image really captures the mental anguish of someone who finds himself in a deep hole.  It must feel that the only way out is to go deeper.  It''s set up and captured beautifully.  The upflung cards, nicely catching the light, are marvelous, putting emotion in motion.  The man''s expression is telling, and driving the entire scene.Personal second favorite of the challenge.   Rich .. i really liked your comment .. especially the bit where you say "it must feel that the only way out is to go deeper." .. that would apply to many addictions .. :( and you know the expression throwing in the towel .. ie. to quit in defeat .. that''s the feeling i get from this pic with the throwing of the cards .. and the man''s expression ..  many congratulations Girish on fourth and such a wonderful photo with such a powerful message .. :)', '2021-03-29 05:51:14.000000', NULL, 0),
